---
import type { Props, Input, Output } from '../.atomic/types/lane-author';
import type { AtomConfig } from '../.atomic/types/authoring';
const { input }: Props = Astro.props;
export const config: AtomConfig<Input, Output> = {
  "description": "Make one bounded change in this attempt's worktree and run its test.",
  "kind": "codex",
  "sandbox": "workspace-write"
};
---

Change only what the task asks for, in the worktree this attempt was given. Keep
the guard working: it names the behaviour the change must not break, and the
step's reviewers read the patch you leave, not your account of it.

Run the test you wrote or changed and report the command you actually ran with
the result it gave. A test you did not run is not reported as passing. Do not
commit, push or merge, and do not report a commit SHA: atomic records the
candidate commit itself once your turn ends, and the reviewers read the patch
atomic computes from it.

Task: {input.task.title}
Guard to keep: {input.task.guard}
Base commit: {input.base}
